# Git hooks and shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# Git runs hooks through its bundled POSIX shell even on Windows. With
# core.autocrlf=true - the default for Git for Windows - a checked-out shell
# script gets CRLF endings, and the shell then fails to parse its own shebang
# with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". Pinning these paths to LF keeps the
# post-merge hook working on a fresh clone regardless of the user's autocrlf
# setting.
scripts/hooks/post-merge text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
